  "proof": "Every l1-ball preprocessor coefficient quadruple is priced after exact linear elimination of coefficients c,d. Sixteen sign/remainder patches parameterize a=\u00b1u,b=\u00b1(1-u)v and remaining l1 mass in signed c or d. Exact bivariate Bernstein subdivision proves a+lambda3*g3+lambda5*g5+lambda7*g7<=z on all patches. Each dual multiplier lies in [-1,1], so the same affine upper bound controls the full residual score of every convex mixture. Higher coefficients only decrease the full residual score; no tail estimate is assumed.",
